            <note corresp="#d24-f16" n="23" xml:id="d24-f16-content">
                <p>On the commercial treaty with Albania, see <!--Volume has not been digitized, no volume id available-->
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1925, volume I, p. 511.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d24-f17" n="24" xml:id="d24-f17-content">
                <p>The Findley–Belcher Amendment to the Food for Peace Act (Section 103 (d) (3)
                    of P.L.–480) forbade the sale of agricultural
                    commodities on credit to “any nation which sells or furnishes or permits ships
                    or aircraft under its registry to transport to or from Cuba or North Vietnam…
                    any equipment, materials, or commodities so long as they are governed by a
                    Communist regime.” (80 Stat. 1527)</p>
            </note>
